#pragma once

/*
 * Where push constants live, spelled once for both APIs.
 *
 * Shader source rather than engine C++, which is why it is not in Common.h
 * beside the shared values: that file is compiled as C++ too, and nothing in
 * engine/ outside the RHI module may name Vulkan — a rule the boundary check
 * enforces on names rather than on includes.
 */

/*
 * A push constant block, spelled for both APIs at once.
 *
 * Both halves are needed and neither is redundant: Vulkan reads the attribute,
 * which is what makes the declaration a push constant rather than an ordinary
 * uniform buffer, and D3D12 reads the register, because root constants appear to
 * a shader as a constant buffer at a b register and it is the root signature
 * rather than the declaration that decides the slot holds constants.
 *
 * Space 7 is reserved for push constants and no bind group may ever use it.
 * That is a portability floor rather than a preference: Vulkan guarantees only
 * sets 0-6 on a 1.4 implementation (maxBoundDescriptorSets is 4 in core and 7
 * for 1.4), and this engine binds four groups, so space 7 is the first number no
 * portable bind group can occupy. It costs nothing on either side — the SPIR-V
 * path reads the attribute and never turns the space into a descriptor set, and
 * D3D12 register spaces are an arbitrary uint32 rather than a budget.
 *
 * A macro rather than the register pasted at each declaration, so that the
 * number exists once. Slang's preprocessor will not expand a function-like macro
 * inside another macro's body, so the space cannot itself be a named constant
 * here.
 */
#define PUSH_CONSTANT(Type, name) [[vk::push_constant]] Type name : register(b0, space7)
